  <keyword>wfdb.iswfdb</keyword>
  <short_description>Probe whether a name is a readable WFDB record.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>tf = wfdb.iswfdb(name)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>name</param_name>
      <param_description>the record to probe, with or without its .hea extension.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>tf</param_name>
      <param_description>true when name.hea is on disk and parses, false otherwise.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>It is true when name names a WFDB record whose header is on disk and parses: the record line and one signal (or segment) line per signal it announces. It reads no samples and never throws, so it is cheap to ask before trying to read a file of an unknown kind.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[if wfdb.iswfdb('100')
  r = wfdb.read('100');
end]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
